// Drain, waste and vent, in building coordinates: the kitchen sink trap arm and its 1 1/2 in vent,
// carried through the bored studs of wall D beside the window, up the wall through both floors, across
// the attic above the insulation and out through the roof at y = 25 ft with a cleanout tee at the
// trap arm. Slope 1/4 in per ft on the trap arm (IPC 704.1).
// The second-floor baths drain to two 3 in horizontal branches in floor bay C-D at y = 28'-10",
// 1/8 in per ft, that meet at a 3 in stack at x = 23'-4". The stack drops through a framed chase in the
// dining room's north-east corner to a 3 in building drain under the slab, 1/4 in per ft, which also takes
// the kitchen sink and leaves through the north stem wall. Vents: a 1 1/2 in vent at the tub end rises in
// wall D and a 2 in vent rises in the partition between the baths; each runs across the attic and out
// through the roof. The primary vanity basins and the hall lavatory vent through air admittance valves.

import { pvc_dwv } from "../../materials.module"

part dwv_piping {
